## How sure it is

Each forecast comes with a range that promises to hold demand {{ nominal|pct(0) }} of the time. From {{ v.conformal.first_fold }} to {{ v.folds.last }}, it held it {{ C.relative.overall.mean|pct(1) }} of the time{% if sides.overall.under %}: less than promised, beyond the uncertainty of the measurement{% elif sides.overall.over %}: more than promised, beyond the uncertainty of the measurement{% else %}: the gap to the promise stays within the uncertainty of the measurement{% endif %}. {% if sides.season.under or sides.decile.under or HBS.under %}It promises too much where demand falls outside it more often than promised, beyond that uncertainty: {{ groups(sides.season.under, sides.decile.under, HBS.under) }}.{% else %}No season, no hour block and no forecast-load decile has demand falling outside it more often than promised beyond that uncertainty.{% endif %} {% if sides.season.over or sides.decile.over or HBS.over %}It is wider than it needs to be where demand stays inside it more often than promised, beyond that uncertainty: {{ groups(sides.season.over, sides.decile.over, HBS.over) }}.{% else %}In no group does demand stay inside it more often than promised beyond that uncertainty.{% endif %}{% if sides.season.under %} The coverage thresholds of {{ groups(sides.season.under, []) }} are drawn from weeks that already had this flaw: the monitor does not flag it as decay.{% endif %} ({{ sec(4) }}{% if sides.season.under %}, {{ sec(8) }}{% endif %})

